4. llama.cpp / ggml — technique of the AVX2 nvfp4 x q8_0 dot product
   Source: https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp (PR #23961, ggml-cpu x86
           quants.c ggml_vec_dot_nvfp4_q8_0)
   Used by Eke Hive: engine/src/cpu/expert_cpu_nvfp4.cpp (W4A8 path,
     gemv_nvfp4_q8_rows_multi / quantize_q8_nvfp4) follows the same method —
     a pshufb table of doubled e2m1 values, int8 activation blocks, maddubs/madd
     integer dot and fp32 block scales — written for Eke Hive's record layout
     (no code copied verbatim; the 16-entry value table is the same).
